.TH "TIMEEVENT.INITTIMEEVENT" "3JS" "April 13, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
TimeEvent.initTimeEvent \- TimeEvent: initTimeEvent() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]TimeEvent.initTimeEvent()\f[B]\f[R] method initializes
the value of a \f[CR]TimeEvent\f[R] created using
\f[CR]Document.createEvent()\f[R].
.PP
This method may only be called before the event has been dispatched via
\f[CR]EventTarget.dispatchEvent()\f[R].
If called multiple times, the final call takes precedence.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] \f[CR]Document.createEvent()\f[R] is deprecated in favor
of event constructors, but \f[CR]TimeEvent\f[R] has no dedicated
constructor.
\f[CR]CustomEvent\f[R] is not a valid replacement, as it does not
produce a \f[CR]TimeEvent\f[R] instance with the interface\(cqs
\f[CR]view\f[R] and \f[CR]detail\f[R] attributes.
.RE
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
initTimeEvent(type)
initTimeEvent(type, view)
initTimeEvent(type, view, detail)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]type\f[R]
A string specifying the event type.
.TP
\f[B]view\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
The \f[CR]Window\f[R] from which the event was generated.
If \f[CR]null\f[R] or omitted, the \f[CR]TimeEvent.view\f[R] attribute
of the event will be \f[CR]null\f[R].
Defaults to \f[CR]null\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]detail\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A \f[CR]long\f[R] providing contextual information about the event.
Defaults to \f[CR]0\f[R].
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Dispatching a repeatEvent
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] evt = document.createEvent(\(dqTimeEvent\(dq);
evt.initTimeEvent(\(dqrepeatEvent\(dq, window, 2);
svgElement.dispatchEvent(evt);
.EE
